---
import PolicyPage from '../components/PolicyPage.astro';
---
<PolicyPage
  title="Returns and cancellations"
  intro="Changing your mind, and what to do if something arrives damaged."
>
  <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>If you are buying as a consumer you may cancel within 14 days of receiving the books, for any reason, and you have a further 14 days to send them back. Tell us by writing to <span class="blank">[the email address to use]</span> — quoting your order reference is enough.</p>
  <p>We refund what you paid, including the standard postage you were charged, within 14 days of the books coming back to us.</p>

  <h2>Sending them back</h2>
  <p>Return postage is paid by <span class="blank">[you or us — say which]</span>. Send them to <span class="blank">[the return address]</span>. Please pack them as they arrived; we can only refund in full if they come back in a condition we could sell.</p>

  <h2>If something is wrong</h2>
  <p>If a book arrives damaged, is not what you ordered, or a set is missing a volume, tell us and we will put it right at our cost. That is separate from changing your mind and is not limited to 14 days.</p>

  <h2>Collection orders</h2>
  <p>Books collected in person are not distance sales, so the 14-day right does not apply — but you are welcome to look at them before you pay.</p>
</PolicyPage>
